      "content": "<h3>1. put, get, remove and the order of pairs</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>V put(K, V);  V get(Object);  V remove(Object)</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> as HashMap</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> New keys are added at the <strong>end</strong> of the order. Putting a key that already exists replaces its value but <strong>keeps its position</strong>. Removing a key just closes the gap.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Each entry is a <code>LinkedHashMap.Entry</code> with <code>before</code> and <code>after</code> links in addition to the bucket link, so adding, removing and reordering are all O(1) pointer changes.</p>",
